      {
        "id": "thm-masking-chain-posterior",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Posterior of a finite masking chain",
        "deps": [
          "def-finite-masking-diffusion-chain",
          "lem-finite-masking-chain-is-well-defined"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "statement": "Let $V$ be a finite nonempty vocabulary, let $m\\notin V$, let $L,N\\ge1$, and let $1=\\alpha_0>\\alpha_1>\\cdots>\\alpha_N=0$ be the survival schedule of the finite masking chain. Fix a clean sequence $x\\in V^L$ and grid indices $0\\le s<t\\le N$. For every state $z_t\\in(V\\cup\\{m\\})^L$ with $\\Pr(Z_t=z_t\\mid X=x)>0$, the conditional law of $Z_s$ given $X=x,Z_t=z_t$ is a product over coordinates. At coordinate $i$, if $z_{t,i}\\in V$, then $Z_{s,i}=z_{t,i}$ with probability one. If $z_{t,i}=m$, then, with $c_{s,t}=(\\alpha_s-\\alpha_t)/(1-\\alpha_t)$, the only possible values are $x_i$ and $m$, with probabilities\n$$\\Pr(Z_{s,i}=x_i\\mid X=x,Z_{t,i}=m)=c_{s,t},\\qquad \\Pr(Z_{s,i}=m\\mid X=x,Z_{t,i}=m)=\\frac{1-\\alpha_s}{1-\\alpha_t}.$$\nThe denominator is positive because $t\\ge1$ implies $\\alpha_t<1$; at $s=0$ the mask posterior has zero mass."
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-finite-masking-path-reversal-factorization",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Finite masking path law factors backward by its posterior rows",
        "deps": [
          "def-finite-masking-diffusion-chain",
          "lem-finite-masking-chain-is-well-defined",
          "thm-masking-chain-posterior"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "dependency_level": 3,
        "statement": "Fix a clean string $x\\in V^L$ and let $q_x$ be the finite forward path law of the absorbing-mask chain. For every path $(z_0,\\ldots,z_N)$ with $q_x(z_0,\\ldots,z_N)>0$, the reversed path probability factors as\n$$q_x(z_0,\\ldots,z_N)=q_x(Z_N=z_N)\\prod_{j=N}^{1}q_x(Z_{j-1}=z_{j-1}\\mid Z_j=z_j).$$\nEach factor on the right is the true one-step posterior conditional on the clean string $x$; the identity is asserted only on positive-probability paths."
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-masked-diffusion-kl-reduces-to-cross-entropy",
